<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mushika dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Mushakas, Mooshika dynasty</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mushika dynasty ruled northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kerala">Kerala</a>, in the region around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ezhimala">Ezhimala</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kannur">Kannur</a> north of the Chera kingdom, in the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">medieval period</a>. Its history is known from inscriptions and from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mushikavamsa">Mushikavamsa</a>, an 11th-century <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanskrit">Sanskrit</a> poem on its kings. The later Kolathiri rulers of Kolathunadu claimed descent from it.</p></div>
